@* NewMemberPage: the form that adds an existing user to a project, at "/projects/{id}/members/new". The page holds
   only the form (a narrow column): the exact user name to add and a "Project admin" choice. Cancel goes back to the
   project and a successful add returns to it. Only whoever may administer the project (a system administrator or a
   project admin of it) gets the form; anybody else sees the not-found message of a missing project.

   Presentation only; state and event handling live in NewMemberPage.razor.cs. There is deliberately no list of users
   to pick from: the user name has to be typed exactly, so nobody can browse the accounts of other projects. When the
   user name cannot be added the message is the same whether the account does not exist or is not usable, and it
   points to the page that creates a new account. The data-interactive marker on the root flips to "true" once the
   live circuit is connected.

   Human factors: (a) one field and one choice; (b) nothing else is on the page, the rare "create a new account"
   action is a button to its own page; (c) the hints say that the name must be exact and what a project admin may do.

   The page body is inside SessionGate, which replaces it with a "Session ended" message when the user is no longer
   valid while the page is open. *@
@page "/projects/{ProjectId:int}/members/new"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@attribute [Authorize]

<PageTitle>Add member - ReviewCenter</PageTitle>

<SessionGate>
<main class="page narrow" data-testid="new-member-page" data-interactive="@InteractiveMarker">
    <nav class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/projects" data-testid="breadcrumb-projects-link">Projects</a>
        @if (Project is not null)
        {
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <a href="/projects/@ProjectId" data-testid="breadcrumb-project-link">@Project.Name</a>
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <span aria-current="page">Add member</span>
        }
    </nav>

    @if (!Loaded)
    {
        <p class="muted" data-testid="new-member-loading">Loading...</p>
    }
    else if (Project is null)
    {
        <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="project-not-found">Project @ProjectId does not exist.</p>
    }
    else
    {
    <h1>Add member</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">Give an existing user access to this project.</p>

    <section class="card">
        @if (ErrorMessage is not null)
        {
            <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="new-member-error">@ErrorMessage</p>
        }
        <form data-testid="new-member-form" @onsubmit="AddMemberAsync">
            <div class="field">
                <label for="new-member-username">User name</label>
                <input id="new-member-username" type="text" maxlength="@ReviewLimits.MaxUsernameLength"
                       autocomplete="off"
                       data-testid="new-member-username-input" @bind="Username" @bind:event="oninput" />
                <p class="muted hint">Type the exact user name of the account.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label>
                    <input type="checkbox" data-testid="new-member-admin-checkbox" @bind="AsProjectAdmin" />
                    Project admin
                </label>
                <p class="muted hint">A project admin also manages the members and repositories of this project.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label>
                    <input type="checkbox" data-testid="new-member-auditor-checkbox" @bind="AsAuditor" />
                    Auditor (read-only)
                </label>
                <p class="muted hint">An auditor can read everything in this project and its audit trail, but cannot change anything or review.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="plan-actions">
                <button type="submit" data-testid="new-member-submit">Add member</button>
                <a class="action outline" href="/projects/@ProjectId" data-testid="new-member-cancel">Cancel</a>
            </div>
        </form>
    </section>

    <p class="muted hint">The person has no account yet?</p>
    <p>
        <a class="action outline" href="/projects/@ProjectId/members/account"
           data-testid="new-member-create-account-link">Create a new account</a>
    </p>
    }
</main>
</SessionGate>
